# 09b round-7 distinguishing ablations of clean payload C7

Payload C7: e59bd312373ca7afacd507a73717b16dfaa0a8f0.
Each ablation changes exactly one behaviour in a detached worktree at C7, runs
packages/kernel/tests/*.test.ts against it, and is reverted before the next.
An ablation is REJECTED when named packet cases fail; that is what makes those cases
distinguishing rather than merely green.

Three ablations are new for the two round-5-review findings. S1 restores the live
`Map.prototype.set` commit path (K11-R5-STATE-01 Map witness); S2 restores live
`Object.freeze` in coordinator construction (K11-R5-STATE-01 freeze witness, with the
replacement live through the later dispatch, as the witness requires); V3 restores the
live-`Object.prototype` plain-object comparison (K11-R5-VAL-03). The remaining six re-prove
representative prior guards still discriminate after the reconstruction; N1/P6 keep their
round-6 contrast (environment vs clone as two independent layers).

